# Samara-ATS: Strategic Product Review

> **Deep-dive audit from product, technical, and business perspectives.**
> Based on a full codebase review of all 16 components, 3 pages, AI libs, SQL migrations, and auth infrastructure.

---

## Current State Summary

| Dimension | What You Have | Maturity |
|---|---|---|
| **Pipeline** | Kanban board with drag-and-drop, 6 stages, real-time sync | ✅ Solid |
| **Candidate Management** | List view, detail panel, pagination, bulk select/reject | ✅ Solid |
| **AI Scoring** | Claude Sonnet compatibility scores (must-have/nice-to-have/salary), risk flags, executive summaries | ✅ Strong differentiator |
| **AI Screening** | Auto-generated interview questions with scorecard, gap probes, risk probes | ✅ Strong differentiator |
| **WhatsApp Integration** | Bilingual templates (ID/EN), stage-aware messaging, bulk broadcasting | ✅ Great for Indonesia market |
| **Import** | Excel/CSV with intelligent column mapping, dedup, progress tracking | ✅ Solid |
| **Analytics** | Pipeline funnel, conversion rates, time-to-hire, dept breakdown | ⚠️ Basic |
| **Auth** | Azure SSO, RBAC (Admin/Manager/Recruiter), multi-tenant RLS | ✅ Enterprise-ready foundations |
| **Audit Trail** | Immutable ledger with triggers, denormalized for fast queries | ✅ Enterprise-grade |
| **TCOW Calculator** | Total cost of worker calculator | ⚠️ Standalone, not integrated |

---

## 🔴 Critical Gaps & Weaknesses

### 1. API Key Exposed in Frontend
```
const ANTHROPIC_KEY = import.meta.env.VITE_ANTHROPIC_KEY
```
In [generateCompatibilityScore.js](file:///c:/Users/Axioo%20Pongo/OneDrive/Desktop/samara-ats/src/lib/generateCompatibilityScore.js#L16), the Anthropic API key is exposed in the client bundle via `VITE_` prefix. Anyone can inspect network traffic and steal your key. **This is a security vulnerability.**

> [!CAUTION]
> Your screening questions already use a Supabase Edge Function proxy (`claude-proxy`). Migrate compatibility scoring to use the same proxy immediately. This is a P0 fix.

### 2. No URL-Based Routing
The app uses `useState('dashboard')` for page switching instead of `react-router-dom` routes — even though `react-router-dom` is already a dependency. This means:
- No deep linking (can't share a URL to a specific candidate or pipeline view)
- No browser back/forward navigation
- No bookmarkable views
- No SEO (irrelevant for internal tools, but signals immaturity)

### 3. No Scheduled/Background Processing
All AI scoring and question generation runs synchronously in the browser. There's no:
- Batch scoring of new candidates
- Nightly re-scoring when role requirements change
- Auto-score on import
- Webhook-triggered workflows

### 4. WhatsApp is Manual Link-Opens, Not API
The WhatsApp integration opens `wa.me` links in new tabs. This is fragile at scale:
- Requires manual click per candidate
- No delivery tracking
- No read receipts
- No conversation history in the ATS
- Breaks above ~20 candidates per session

### 5. No Candidate Deduplication Beyond Import
Import checks for duplicate applications, but there's no global candidate merge/dedup — candidates applied through different channels will create separate records.

### 6. No Email Communication
The entire communication layer is WhatsApp-only. There's no:
- Email templates
- Automated email sequences
- Calendar invite generation for interviews
- Offer letter delivery

---

## 🟡 Product Gaps (High Impact)

### 7. Analytics Are Static Snapshots
Current analytics recompute from raw data on every page load. Missing:
- **Time-series trends** (pipeline velocity over weeks/months)
- **Source effectiveness** (which channels produce best hires?)
- **Recruiter performance** (applications processed per recruiter)
- **Role fill rate** by department
- **Drop-off analysis** (where in the pipeline do candidates fall off?)
- **Cost-per-hire** (integrate with TCOW)

### 8. No Interview Scheduling
There's no calendar integration. Recruiters must manually schedule interviews via WhatsApp, then remember to update the stage. This is the **#1 workflow bottleneck** in most ATS systems.

### 9. No Offer Management
The "Offer" stage exists but there's no:
- Offer letter generation
- Approval workflows
- Counter-offer tracking
- Offer acceptance/decline flow

### 10. Notes System Is Invisible
Notes are being written during import, but the `CandidateDetail` panel doesn't surface a timeline/activity feed. Recruiter notes, stage changes, score changes — all should be in a single chronological feed.

### 11. No Configurable Pipeline Stages
Stages are hardcoded as `['New', 'Screening', 'Interview', 'Offer', 'Hired', 'Rejected']`. Enterprise customers will demand custom stages, sub-stages, and parallel tracks.

