## ⚔️ Differentiation Strategy vs. Existing Players

### Competitive Landscape (Indonesia/SEA)

| Competitor | Strength | Weakness |
|---|---|---|
| **Kalibrr** | Job board + basic ATS | No AI, generic pipeline |
| **Mekari Talenta** | HRIS + payroll | ATS is an afterthought, no AI scoring |
| **Workable** | Full-featured global ATS | Expensive, not localized for Indonesia |
| **Greenhouse** | Enterprise-grade | $6k+/year, overkill for SMBs, no WhatsApp |
| **Lever** | Great UX | No SEA focus, no local comms integration |

### Your Unfair Advantages

1. **WhatsApp-native communication** — No major ATS player has WhatsApp as a first-class channel. In Indonesia, 93% of recruiters use WhatsApp. Build the best WhatsApp recruiting experience.

2. **AI scoring with local context** — Your prompts already encode Lombok-specific signals (origin-based risk, IDR salary, local market awareness). Competitors using generic AI can't match this.

3. **"Lombok First" hiring policy** — This is not just a filter, it's a philosophic differentiator. Position Samara-ATS as the **ethical ATS for local-first hiring** — ESG-conscious enterprises will pay premium.

4. **Hospitality domain expertise** — Your role/department structures, TCOW calculator, and scoring prompts are tailored for hospitality+construction. Go deep on this vertical before going wide.

### Differentiation Positioning

> **"The AI-native ATS built for Southeast Asian hiring — WhatsApp-first, local-first, and 10x faster than legacy tools."**

